hen allow you to  come down to a lateral resolution of 20  nanometers  great thank you  next question  given the odor specific activation of  hdb fibers within ob  and the fact that the hdb does not  receive input direct input from ob  along which pathway is ob output relayed  into hdb  yeah this is a biological question  it's a good question actually  the hdb does not receive direct input  from the ob and the question is how does  the how does how is this in for this  other information related to the hdb and  we did also  monotron synaptic tracing and found that  the  ob project into the olfactory amygdala  and the effector amygdala project into  the  paraventricular nucleus and from the  paraventricular nucleus then goes the  projection to the hdb which is then  related into the factory bulb  wow  right thank you  and it looks like we have time for one  more question  why do you not image just the complete  sample with high resolution  yeah i mean as as we mentioned and as  you can see in this table  going with a really high resolution to  image the complete sample will be just  like too much data that will not give  you actually more information that the  one that you can  go get if you like kind of partialize  the the your imaging session so i think  that the advantage of this kind of  lighting  systems the one that the one that we  show like the place where you can change  objective  plus the  the fact that you you have like an  entire  um  neuronal circuit containing in in your  sample  is the one that that  actually allows you to get all the  necessary information but in in a let's  say  a smarter way  all right  well thank you dr schwartz professor  kubick mr rodriguez do you have any  closing statements for our audience  yeah  maybe that  since some years we are working on these  techniques and developing our  microscopes in order to optimize that  martin is working on the labeling and  this is uh juan is uh doing the  experiments and the data evaluation so